From 67246d4422ec76477ed3c077c150044bd4f1b82c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:07:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 40/42] perf(qsa): split-K for the QSA indexer MQA scoring
 kernel

Port of Lesilva's patch 0003 (QSA indexer split-K). Deep long-context chunks
otherwise launch about 8 CTAs on 188 SMs. With split-K, several CTAs per row
block each score a disjoint range of the block's key tiles. Every logit is
still produced by exactly one CTA with the same tile arithmetic, so results are
bit-identical to split=1; only the grid grows.

SGLANG_QSA_MQA_SPLITK=auto (default) picks a power-of-two split that aims for a
few waves while keeping a minimum number of key tiles per CTA. =1 disables it;
any other integer forces that split.

Credit: Lesilva (qwen38-flashnext-nvfp4-kv).
